id: SceneVariants
name: ᝯㄝₓ Scene Variants
metadata:
  description: "A scene is often in your library twice: the whole thing, and a cut out of it. Stash has no way to say the two are the same work, so this plugin works it out and gives the scene page a tab that shows you.\n\nOpen any scene and there is a Siblings tab beside Details, File Info and Edit. It lists every other scene sharing this one's stash-id - each a link, with its resolution and running time, longest first - and where there is nothing to list it says why. Nothing is written to your library at any point: the tab is one query and a list of links.\n\nName your full-length and partial-length tags below and each row says which it is, with the full-length ones sorted to the top - that is the question the tab exists to answer, and the tags are the cheap half of it. Leave them empty and the tab still lists the siblings, just without saying which is which.\n\nThe stash-id is the only evidence used. A scene that never got one, or whose siblings never got one, gets a tab that says so; matching on titles and on shared performers is not built yet, so about two scenes in three have nothing to list today. A scene carrying both tags at once is shown in red, because the two are meant to be exclusive.\n\nRequires Stash 0.28.0 or newer: the tab is added through the scene page's own plugin extension points, so there is no version of it that works without them."
